      "output": "C03 review complete. Report delivered at `runs/mw_protocol_v3_v1_1_application_review_20260913/reviewer_scratch/REPORT.md`.\n\n**Verdict:** the frozen 15-file candidate holds under independent challenge — 49 of 50 independent probe checks passed, and every lifecycle claim in the assignment was reproduced with synthetic HTTP + temp SQLite. One low-severity frozen-code defect, one low-severity UI observation, and three adjacent-layer risks to carry into the pending App-mount phase. No final product acceptance claimed.\n\n**What was verified independently:**\n\n- **Hashes:** all 15 files match `artifact_manifest.json` in both the snapshot and the live tree, re-confirmed after all review activity (source untouched).\n- **Lifecycle (23/23):** start persists the run before any dispatch; GET leaves event and reservation counts unchanged; same-input re-POST/execute reuses the run with zero extra model calls; known-invalid initial → exactly one correction; crash between initial and correction recovers via re-POST with exactly the missing call; initial and correction timeouts both end `blocked` and are never redispatched; selection order and duplicate ids don't change the seed; superseded ids fail closed. Two threads resuming the same run on real SQLite produced exactly one physical generation with no overlapping HTTP calls.\n- **HTTP boundary (12/13):** 202/404/409/422 all return the Chinese envelopes; unadmitted projects never create the DB file.\n- **Probe restoration:** `RestoredZhipuProbePolicy` loads the real approved receipt (`runs/mw_protocol_v3_1r6_glm_transport_20260905/product_probe_attempt.json`), pins its hash, skips the probe for the registry-bound identity, and rejects mismatching receipts; `effective_reasoning_effort` honestly stays `not_reported_by_server`.\n- **UI (10/10):** import/correction double-click guards work; invalid list payloads, transport failures, and unshapely correction responses all degrade to Chinese guidance with refresh; clear-to-未注明 flags interact correctly with typing; unmount/project-switch aborts are clean.\n\n**Findings:** D1 (Low) — `GET /research-intake/{id}` naming an existing correction-run id raises unhandled `GraphPlanBindingError` → raw 500 outside the envelope (`research_intake.py:41-50` / `seed_coordinator.py:50`; repro = probe H4b; fix = map it to the existing 404). D2 (Low) — 准备写作材料 has no synchronous ref guard, so double-click fires `onPrepare` twice; neutralized by the non-frozen workspace's ref guard plus API idempotency. R1 (Medium, pending wiring) — a `running` job orphaned by a server restart has no UI recovery path since the workspace blocks re-prepare while running; the frozen API already supports recovery-by-re-POST. R2/R3 (Low) — per-request artifact-store instances don't share the manifest lock, and each dispatch holds a threadpool thread up to 600 s.\n\n**Scope notes:** `main.py:591` mounts the chain without `seed_coordinator_factory`, so the intake router and restored probe policy are test-only until wired — matching the declared App-mount-pending scope, not counted as defects. Code-level lazy-flow estimate: ~6 clicks and 0 required free-text fields for the base intake path, within the ≤20/≤5 budget; native file-dialog acceptance remains pending.",
